his accommodation overnight at the lodge. Hawken and the Canadian agreed. The next day, the man led them out to his vehicle, a white Subaru station wagon with custom bull bars. They explained that he'd borrowed the car from his cousin, hence why he didn't know how to use certain features, such as the car stereo. There was also some camping and fishing gear in the back, which the man said belonged to his cousin.
